**Feature 1: AI Schema Mapping**
- Description: *"When you connect your MongoDB database, the app reads your collections and sends the structure to AI. The AI figures out how to turn your MongoDB documents into proper PostgreSQL tables — flattening nested objects, splitting arrays into separate tables, and choosing the right data types."*
- Why it matters: *Saves hours of manual mapping. Understands business logic, not just raw types.*

**Feature 2: Risk Report**
- Description: *"Before any migration runs, the app scans your schema and data for potential problems. It categorizes them as Critical (will fail), Warning (may cause issues), or Info (safe but worth knowing)."*
- Examples shown: *"Your 'items' array will need a separate table" / "45 users have no email — column can't be NOT NULL"*

**Feature 3: Dry Run Mode**
- Description: *"Click 'Dry Run' and the app simulates the entire migration without writing a single permanent row to your database. It tells you exactly how many rows would be migrated, how many would be skipped, and why."*
- Why it matters: *Builds confidence. You know what will happen before it happens.*

**Feature 4: Rollback Script**
- Description: *"Every migration automatically generates a rollback SQL script. If something goes wrong after migration, run this script and your database goes back to its original state."*
- Example rollback SQL shown as a code block.

**Feature 5: Live Progress Tracking**
- Description: *"While your migration runs, you see a live progress bar and a real-time log. You know exactly which table is being migrated, how many rows have been copied, and if any rows were skipped."*

**Feature 6: 100% Local Execution**
- Description: *"The app runs entirely on your Windows PC. Your database passwords never leave your machine. There's no cloud server, no account, no subscription. Just download and run."*

**Feature 7: ERD Diagram Export**
- Description: *"After connecting to any database, the app automatically generates a visual Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD) — a map showing all your tables/collections, their fields, and the relationships (foreign keys) between them. You can view it inside the app or download it as a PNG image."*
- Why it matters: *Instantly understand a complex database at a glance. Great for documentation and team presentations.*
- What you'll see: A visual diagram with boxes for each table connected by lines showing foreign key relationships. Hovering a line shows the FK constraint name.

**Feature 8: AI Schema Health Score**
- Description: *"Before migration, the AI examines your source database and gives it a health score from 0 to 100. It flags specific problems — type inconsistencies, missing indexes, sparse fields — and tells you exactly what's impacting the score and how to fix it."*
- Why it matters: *Gives you actionable insight into your schema quality before you commit to a migration. No other free migration tool does this.*
- Example output shown:
  ```
  Schema Health: 71 / 100
  🔴 -15pts  orders.items has inconsistent object structure
  🟡 -10pts  users.phone has 3 different data types
  🟡 -4pts   products collection has no indexes
  ✅ +0pts   users.email present in 99.8% of documents
  ```

**Feature 9: Partial Migration**
- Description: *"By default, the app migrates your entire database. But if you only need to move specific collections, or only data from a certain time period, you can use the Partial Migration filter. Toggle it on, select which collections to include, and optionally set a date range."*
- Why it matters: *Real migrations are rarely all-or-nothing. This makes the tool practical for staging environments, incremental moves, and data archiving.*

**Feature 10: Schema Version History**
- Description: *"Every schema change you make through the Schema Update Assistant is recorded with a timestamp. You can view the full history of changes made to any database, and download the rollback script for any past change — even ones made weeks ago."*
- Why it matters: *Like Git for your database. Know exactly what changed, when, and how to undo it.*

**Feature 11: Demo Mode**
- Description: *"Don't have a database ready? No problem. Click 'Try with Sample Data' on the home screen and the app loads a pre-bundled e-commerce database instantly. You go through the full 8-step migration wizard on real-looking data — no installation of MongoDB or PostgreSQL needed."*
- Why it matters: *Evaluators, professors, and anyone who downloads the app can experience a full migration in under 2 minutes without any setup. Perfect for demos and presentations.*

**Feature 12: Estimated Time Remaining**
- Description: *"During a live migration, the progress bar shows not just the percentage complete, but also the current processing speed (rows per second) and an estimated time remaining. You never have to wonder how long it will take."*
- Why it matters: *Large migrations can take minutes. A visible ETA means the user can step away confidently instead of staring at the screen.*

