## 🟢 Lower Priority — Known Limitations (Accepted, Documented)

| Limitation | What it means | Our stance |
|---|---|---|
| **`electron-store` is not encrypted** | Saved connection strings (with passwords) are stored in a plain JSON file on disk | We note this in Settings with: *"Saved credentials are stored locally and unencrypted. Do not save production credentials on a shared PC."* |
| **No real-time / CDC migration** | New data written to MongoDB during migration is not captured | Documented limitation; user is warned before migration starts |
| **PostgreSQL → MongoDB is harder** | Reconstructing embedded documents from JOINs (Workflow B) is significantly more complex to implement than the Mongo→PG direction | Acknowledged — Workflow B may have a slightly simpler implementation for the FYP (e.g., embedding only verified 1:N tables, not all JOINs) |
| **No MySQL / SQLite support** | Only MongoDB and PostgreSQL are supported | Explicitly stated on the Download page and Features page |
| **No user authentication** | The app has no login system | Not needed — it's a local desktop app, not a multi-user platform |
| **Free AI tier rate limits** | Heavy use (many migrations in a short time) may trigger 429 rate limit errors | Fallback rule engine activates automatically; user sees `[⚡ Auto Rule-Mapped]` badge |
| **Code signing / SmartScreen** | Unsigned .exe shows Windows warning on first run | Download page includes bypass instructions |
| **Windows only** | The `.exe` only runs on Windows 10/11 64-bit | Explicitly stated on the Download page. No macOS or Linux version is planned. |

